  "answer": "I'll treat this as a storefront cart feature and start by reading the feature playbook and the cart API so the quantity limit is modeled from the existing cart shape.The cart write path and merchant config are being traced in parallel. I'll keep mapping the REST controllers so the design can land on the real mutation methods.The cart writes all go through one facade, and merchant configuration is read from the database on each call. I'll put the limit in that facade so a config change applies on the next request, and I'll reject the request before any line is saved.A storefront cart line is now capped by the store merchant configuration key `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY`, or 99 when that key is missing. `POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi` read that value on each request, and they return HTTP 400 without saving when the resulting line would be above the cap. A quantity of 0 still removes the line. Adding to an existing line counts the sum. Model the domain put the rule in `CartLineQuantityPolicy`. Boundary discipline rejects the request before any cart write. Laziness protocol kept the check in the existing cart facade.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=CartLineQuantityPolicyTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 from the running storefront cart API, and that a rejected request leaves the saved cart unchanged\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration test that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY on a store and calls the cart endpoints\"]}The traces from [Cart write paths](6b3e75f4-c5fb-4e12-b6eb-68c5465fd1cc) and [Merchant configuration](559d668c-6e9c-4d4b-bb02-5826e39894fb) match the change already in place. Storefront writes go through `POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi`. The cap is read from `MERCHANT_CONFIGURATION` on each request, which is not cached. Quantity 0 is still allowed, and an add to an existing line is checked as a sum. No further code change.",
